    {
      "id": "claim_b64a23473aa34ef39f94d9b8547f542d",
      "statement": "@ulabase/cli (^0.14.0 dev dependency) provisions a Ulabase service via ulabase login and ulabase setup commands; setup files use defineSetup/step DSL with check/apply pairs, and --dry-run runs checks only to report what is missing. ulabase.setup.ts's step list (in run order) installs the accounts feature (treating 409 Plugin already installed as success), sets branding's name to APP_NAME via read-modify-write so console-set color and logo survive, configures accounts with frontend-url/frontend-app-url set to APP_URL and feature toggles derived from the same environment.dev.ts the app imports (registration and verification both from emailRegistration, then password-reset, invitations, oauth), adds Google OAuth credentials from GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET via fromEnv only when not already stored and only when the app's flags offer Google, adds APP_URL to the origin-allowlist's allowed-origins (added, never replaced), and finally runs the exported appPointsAtService step which writes the service URL into the apiUrl line of environment.dev.ts so a half-finished setup leaves the connect-your-service screen rather than a failing sign-up page.",
