    {
      "id": "claim_2fdd7216bf484cc5a457fb99df0ac736",
      "statement": "The OpenWiki GitHub Actions workflow runs on a nightly cron schedule (17 7 * * * i.e. 07:17 UTC, deliberately off the hour), on push of version tags matching [0-9]+.[0-9]+.[0-9]+, and on manual workflow_dispatch with an optional message input passed to OpenWiki as a per-run instruction. On scheduled runs it gates on changed paths: it finds the last commit touching openwiki/ and counts files changed since it excluding openwiki/, AGENTS.md, and CLAUDE.md, stopping before any API spend when nothing else changed; release-tag and manual runs always proceed. It checks out main (even on tag runs, where a detached HEAD cannot open a PR), runs openwiki code --update --print (or --init when no wiki exists) with OPENWIKI_MODEL_ID xiaomi/mimo-v2.6-pro via OpenRouter pinned to the deepinfra upstream and NODE_OPTIONS importing .github/openwiki-retry.mjs, then creates a PR on branch openwiki/update limited to openwiki/, AGENTS.md, and CLAUDE.md which is auto-merged (squash, delete branch). openwiki-retry.mjs wraps fetch to retry OpenRouter /chat/completions requests that answer 429 with backoff delays of 30, 60, 120, 240, and 480 seconds, returning the 429 as-is after the final 480s attempt; only requests with a replayable string body are retried, and DeepInfra's 429 engine_overloaded responses (no Retry-After) would otherwise be fatal in the OpenWiki planner.",
      "evidence": [
